      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n        \"Courtiers\",\n        \"Musicians\",\n        \"Buffoons\",\n        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n        \"Improvisatori\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a gruesome plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to seal himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape the contagion. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their decor—host a lavish masked ball, illuminated only by firelight from external tripods casting eerie glows through the glass, except in the final black chamber where blood-red windows and black velvet tapestries create a ghastly atmosphere dominated by a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all merriment. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death, with a corpse-like mask and blood-drenched robes, enters unchallenged, walking slowly through all seven rooms until confronting Prince Prospero in the blue chamber; the prince, enraged, pursues the figure with a dagger but collapses dead upon reaching the black room, where the figure is found to be empty, revealing the Red Death itself has infiltrated the abbey, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\