  },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"live\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 7580,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...f-subdued laughter floats after them as they depart. And now again the music swells, and the dreams live, and writhe to and fro more merrily than ever, taking hue from the many tinted windows through whic...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: to exist (LIV); in real time (LYVE)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"close\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 1772,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...there was wine. All these and security were within. Without was the \\\"Red Death.\\\" It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad,...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: nearby (KLOHS); to shut (KLOHZ)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"produce\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 5609,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...s and folly, and made whispering vows, each to the other, that the next chiming of the clock should produce in them no similar emotion; and then, after the lapse of sixty minutes, (which embrace three thousa...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: vegetables (PROH-doos); to make (pruh-DOOS)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 11611,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"glossary\": null,\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"structure\": {\n      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n      \"has_titles\": false,\n      \"has_parts\": false,\n      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n    },\n    \"plot_summary\": {\n      \"plot_summary\": \"In the face of a merciless plague known as the Red Death—a disease marked by bleeding from the pores and swift, agonizing death—Prince Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and self-imposed isolation, retreats with a thousand courtiers into a secluded, fortified abbey. The abbey, a labyrinth of seven opulently decorated rooms, each distinguished by a different color and illuminated by firelight from tripods that cast shifting shadows through stained-glass windows, becomes a sanctuary of decadence and denial. The prince, obsessed with preserving his own life and status, hosts a lavish masked ball, attempting to drown out the terror of the outside world with music, revelry, and illusion. The atmosphere is one of eerie beauty, especially in the final black chamber, adorned with blood-red windows and black velvet tapestries, where a massive ebony clock chimes each hour, halting all merriment and reminding the guests of their fleeting time.\\n\\nAs the night progresses, the mood shifts from gaiety to unease. The arrival of a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—complete with a corpse-like mask and robes stained with blood—shatters the illusion of safety. The figure moves silently through the seven rooms, unchallenged, a macabre specter among the revelers. Prince Prospero, enraged by the intrusion and the violation of his sanctuary, pursues the figure with a dagger, driven by pride and fear. His pursuit leads him through the increasingly ominous rooms, culminating in the black chamber, where he collapses dead upon arrival. The figure, revealed to be empty, is not a man but the embodiment of the plague itself, having infiltrated the abbey under the guise of a guest. The clock stops at midnight, and darkness consumes the abbey, signaling the end of all life within.\\n\\nThe story concludes with the complete annihilation of the revelers, each succumbing to the Red Death as the final act of the plague’s inevitability. The prince’s attempt to escape death through wealth, isolation, and spectacle proves futile, underscoring the futility of denying mortality. The narrative reveals that the Red Death was never an external threat to be walled out—it was always within, manifesting not as a physical invader but as a consequence of arrogance and denial. The relationship between the prince and his courtiers is one of mutual indulgence and shared delusion, bound together by a fragile illusion of safety. The turning point occurs when the figure enters, not as a threat from outside, but as the fulfillment of the very fear the abbey was meant to escape. The resolution is not redemption or survival, but total and inevitable loss, where the boundaries between life, death, and illusion dissolve into silence.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"timing\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 15.54,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"15.5s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 323.05,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"5m 23s\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 26.77,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"26.8s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 0.0,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"0.0s\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 76.14,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"1m 16s\"\n      },\n      \"total\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 446.77,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"7m 27s\"\n      },\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-01-19 06:13:16\",\n      \"ended_at\": \"2026-01-19 06:20:43\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"low_confidence_items\": [],\n  \"_analysis_metadata\": {\n    \"analyzed_at\": \"2026-01-19T06:20:54.254240\",\n    \"analyzer_version\": \"0.2.0\",\n    \"pipeline\": \"multi-agent\",\n    \"llm_model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n    \"llm_provider\": \"ollama\",\n    \"analysis_duration_seconds\": 457.5\n  },\n  \"_profiling\": {\n    \"stages\": [\n      {\n        